        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                "word": "surabondance",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3130dfc6-82a4-4dd2-8322-6a2653566b7a",
                        "entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "surabondances"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                        "entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Très grande abondance, abondance qui va au-delà du nécessaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77194b47-7fa4-4e80-8293-3b239ebaee32",
                                "sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                                "text": "Le comte des Essarts , parti de Versailles le 9 Février, pour se rendre à sa terre des Essarts, ayant trouvé que la route de traverse de Damville aux Essarts étoit impraticable & dangereuse par la surabondance des neiges, se vit forcé de rester plusieurs jours à Damville chez le procureur fiscal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3dc4d78e-bcf5-42ac-97e4-f73bdfa7ab71",
                                "sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                                "text": "Quand je pense au gâchis des tropiques, au désordre des fleurs, des fruits, à ce luxe, cette profusion, cette surabondance scandaleuse jetée par la terre à pleins bras au premier venu, qui n’a rien fait pour ça, ne l’a pas mérité !..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bae4df43-af57-4271-a921-b2bed72fbc17",
                                "sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                                "text": "Mais à l'âge de la sérénité cette préoccupation ne se pose plus : l'homme est débordé par la surabondance des possibles qui redondent des valeurs qu'il contemple, si du moins sa destinée est réussie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d98a4491-1da5-4443-958c-aecaecdb4cdf",
                                "sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                                "text": "À un point tel qu’un des défis majeurs auxquels nous faisons face aujourd’hui est la surabondance de l’information."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f62e461-e50f-41eb-88d8-77465708319c",
                                "sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                                "text": "Comble de bonheur, elle était accompagnée de sa stagiaire, belle brune grassouillette dotée d'une surabondance mammaire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29d208d0-9aaa-4a63-b852-7c9a31d26a58",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                        "source_sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                        "target_lang_word": "Überfülle",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "569139d1-5c9c-4acb-b421-a624a4d84c53",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                        "source_sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                        "target_lang_word": "overabundance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overabundance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd03a07a-b744-3173-9119-b63be0e1027d",
                                        "entry_id": "313f2f36-b680-3462-9bc7-17fa8bc63a5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An excess of what is needed or is appropriate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17a1880e-57bf-4ac2-828a-fc297229d83d",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                        "source_sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                        "target_lang_word": "superabundance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "superabundance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3afe83bb-eb11-32b5-9fb1-986016d910e9",
                                        "entry_id": "cdf169c7-2d07-302e-a924-6b99d0131885",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extreme abundance; abundance to a vast degree that seems almost excessive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f012e3d-6fce-44b4-b749-a4b6f0768d0a",
                                                "sense_id": "3afe83bb-eb11-32b5-9fb1-986016d910e9",
                                                "text": "We have not merely an abundance, but a superabundance of enemies at this time; they will need to stand in line to disagree with us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e25a192-cff8-4d3c-944a-608932e8c890",
                                                "sense_id": "3afe83bb-eb11-32b5-9fb1-986016d910e9",
                                                "text": "Perhaps very young girls, who do not know what to do with a superabundance of affection, run up a kind of romantic liking for each other; but it never lasts—one good-looking young man would break up all the female friendships that ever were formed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd15c41a-c51e-418d-a823-878aca160110",
                                                "sense_id": "3afe83bb-eb11-32b5-9fb1-986016d910e9",
                                                "text": "We behold the face of nature bright with gladness, we often see superabundance of food; we do not see, or we forget, that the birds which are idly singing round us mostly live on insects or seeds, and are thus constantly destroying life; or we forget how largely these songsters, or their eggs, or their nestlings, are destroyed by birds and beasts of prey; we do not always bear in mind, that though food may be now superabundant, it is not so at all seasons of each recurring year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b46e2e4-5cc9-4f3d-b264-05a882055da9",
                                                "sense_id": "3afe83bb-eb11-32b5-9fb1-986016d910e9",
                                                "text": "My friends, do you realize the meaning of VITAL POWER? Have you ever experienced that superabundance of health which breeds an intense satisfaction with life and all living things?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "332db918-d924-4e6c-8065-3d7020195da8",
                                                "sense_id": "3afe83bb-eb11-32b5-9fb1-986016d910e9",
                                                "text": "Long silence not result of lack of interest. Lots of sickness, moving, superabundance of work, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e41a0b83-356e-4d9d-8027-e6d7a36621c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fe4b74d-323c-3deb-bc2a-7b4a152584ee",
                        "source_sense_id": "9384d9ef-9023-3528-8194-993aaacef714",
                        "target_lang_word": "superfluity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "superfluity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "606d2d87-c2b5-34da-8a84-ffdd349a9f67",
                                        "entry_id": "748855df-eae0-39a7-8cbd-2d99e972ba16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being superfluous; overflowingness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4321d84-68fd-4480-86ea-134a59730072",
                                                "sense_id": "606d2d87-c2b5-34da-8a84-ffdd349a9f67",
                                                "text": "Each stores has its own storekeeper, a clerk who specializes in organizing his department so that there is not a superfluity of one article and a scarcity of another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                        "entry_id": "748855df-eae0-39a7-8cbd-2d99e972ba16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something superfluous, as a luxury."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1286939-6a63-4c01-b44c-8ca08102f99c",
                                                "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                                "text": "As they had almost all the conveniencies of life within themselves, they seldom visited towns or cities in search of superfluity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c7e08c6-96ab-4cc6-a7e7-34fb6c5ae7f4",
                                                "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                                "text": "I really doubt whether there be such a thing as a heart in the world: perhaps, after all, it is only an elegant superfluity kept for the use of poets. Certainly we have no use for it here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bf49424-0187-469b-8491-b212e494af07",
                                                "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                                "text": "It is to be presumed that Miss Blanche Amory had more than one rose in her bouquet, and why should not the kind young creature give out of her superfluity, and make as many partners as possible happy?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                        "entry_id": "748855df-eae0-39a7-8cbd-2d99e972ba16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Collective noun for a group of nuns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d618e88-e27d-41c2-ad0e-2942b764d4fd",
                                                "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                                "text": "These probably mark the dwelling of a colony, or to speak more precisely, according to Dame Juliana Berners, a superfluity of nuns from Godstow, which nunnery had a cell there, and was patron of the living."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10703335-6009-492e-ba28-742591f21b6c",
                                                "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                                "text": "Alice put Anna back on the shelf and turned up the volume on the TV, where a local news reporter was imparting a salutary tale of woe involving a superfluity of nuns who'd got into a scrape at a crab festival."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f2293ae-5095-48af-8ceb-992e81c43e6a",
                                                "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                                "text": "[…] That man could charm the panties off a superfluity of nuns.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
